# Upstream files this integration deliberately does not ship.
#
# eye is a module inside TibaDesk, not a product with a public face of its own.
# It brings sixteen marketing pages and a public layout that present it as a
# separate eye clinic website — a second website alongside TIBADesk-website,
# reached at /apps/eye/about, /apps/eye/contact and so on. The module opens its
# own panel instead; see resources/js/components/App.jsx.
#
# These pages are removed rather than merely unrouted because they cannot be
# left in place. Any future sync restores them from upstream, so a bare deletion
# in apps/ would not survive, and a link added later would put a working public
# site back on screen.
#
# Paths are relative to the application root, and are checked by
# bin/sync-apps.sh --verify — which is what catches a wrong prefix here.
# One path per line. Blank lines and # comments are ignored.

resources/js/layouts/PublicLayout.jsx

resources/js/pages/public/AboutPage.jsx
resources/js/pages/public/BlogIndexPage.jsx
resources/js/pages/public/BlogShowPage.jsx
resources/js/pages/public/BookAppointmentPage.jsx
resources/js/pages/public/ContactPage.jsx
resources/js/pages/public/FacilityPage.jsx
resources/js/pages/public/FAQPage.jsx
resources/js/pages/public/HomePage.jsx
resources/js/pages/public/OutreachPage.jsx
resources/js/pages/public/PartnersPage.jsx
resources/js/pages/public/PrivacyPage.jsx
resources/js/pages/public/ProductsPage.jsx
resources/js/pages/public/ServicesPage.jsx
resources/js/pages/public/TeamPage.jsx
resources/js/pages/public/TermsPage.jsx
resources/js/pages/public/WhyChooseUsPage.jsx

# The old static marketing site's script. Nothing loads it — not the SPA shell,
# not a standalone page — and it only ever operated on the markup those pages
# were built from. It came back with the site's removal by association, not
# because the panel needs it.
public/assets/js/main.js
# The remnants of the same site's shell: a home page, an about page and a
# services page at the top of resources/js, the header and footer they share,
# and the SEO component that stamped meta tags onto them. Upstream has already
# unwired all seven — nothing routes to them and nothing imports them, which is
# why they are merely dead rather than a second website. They are removed so
# they cannot be relinked later, and so the next person reading this repository
# does not find a plausible-looking home page for the module and take it for
# the intended entry point.
#
# components/pdf/Footer is a different file and is used by the report and invoice
# PDFs. It is not listed here and must not be.
resources/js/Home.jsx
resources/js/About.jsx
resources/js/Services.jsx
resources/js/Footer.jsx
resources/js/Navbar.jsx
resources/js/Navbar.css
resources/js/components/SEO.jsx
